hen he reaches the pit, he falls.\n\nWith ~87px of airborne travel per 105px cycle, there's ~18px of ground travel between landings. The chance of that 18px window aligning exactly with the pit is low but not zero.\n\nAlternative: hold A continuously? No, SMB requires release to re-jump.\n\nHmm, alternatively: for pits, having high speed helps — running speed 2.5px/f with a jump gives ~87px horizontal, enough to clear a 3-tile (24px) pit trivially if the jump starts near the edge.\n\nI think the death was because he was slow/stuck. Let me restore slot 2 (x=845) and try again with a tighter cycle.\n\nActually, wait: at the time of death, $0086 was moving 183,208,233,2 — that's 25px per 10 frames = 2.5px/f = full run speed. Good.\n\nHmm, but then it stopped at 225 and he fell. So he ran full speed into a pit and couldn't jump because the jump cycle had him on the ground at that moment.\n\nTo be safer: jump immediately when landing (minimal ground time). Cycle: 16 right+b+a (jump) then 8 right+b (release, land, immediately next jump)... hmm, but the jump needs A released for a few frames.\n\nActually in SMB, to jump you press A; if you hold A, the jump continues (higher). You can't re-jump while holding. Sequence: press A for ~20 frames (full jump), release for ~8, press again. Cycle 28 frames. Jump spacing = 2.5*28 = 70px. Airtime ~35 frames... hmm, a full jump lasts ~35 frames; if A is released at 20, the jump still continues but with reduced height.\n\nLet me think: rise takes ~16 frames (A held), fall takes ~16 frames. Total ~32 frames. So press A for 16, release for 16, press again. Cycle 32, jump spacing at 2.5px/f = 80px, horizontal air travel ~80px. So essentially continuous jumping with no ground time. \n\nLet me use cycle: {right,b,a} 16, {right,b} 16 → 32 frames.\n\nHmm, but tapping A for 16 frames gives full rise. Good.\n\nActually there's a subtlety: pressing A on the ground triggers a jump; if pressed while airborne, nothing (unless it's a \"jump\" input buffer). Fine.\n\nLet's try: from slot 2 (x=845), run with cycle 16/16 for 600 frames ≈ 1500px. But that might overshoot the flagpole... no, level is 3200px. From 845 + 1500 = 2345. Hmm, we want to stop at the Koopa.\n\nBut our immediate problem is the pit at 1249.\n\nActually let me reconsider: maybe I should look at the screen more carefully. Let me restore slot 2 and take a screenshot to see what's ahead.\n\nPlan:\n1. load_state 2\n2. screenshot (see the area)\n3. play with a tight jump cycle, but in shorter stretches (300 frames) checking screenshots.\n\nLet's do it.\n\nActually also worth noting: at slot 2 the state was mid-jump at x=845, TIME 261, score 200, lives 10 (we set 9 → 10 lives). After the death, lives = 8. Restoring slot 2 restores lives=9 too. Good.\n\nLet me load and screenshot."}
