{"type":"text","text":"Done — both mapping sheets are recorded and promoted. Summary:\n\n## Koopa Troopa — `sprite` id `koopa`\n**Reach:** from the 1‑1 start, played right with a run+jump cycle past the four pipes. The Koopa was at level x 1652 (page `$006E`+1 = 6, low `$0087`+1 = 116), screen origin (16,185), walking left.\n\n**Proof (`list_sprites`):** a 6‑entry OAM group (slots 40–45), one 16×24 metasprite, all sprite palette 5, every entry `flip_h`, none behind background:\n- `$A5` (+0,+0) head · `$FC` (+8,+0) blank filler · `$A7` (+0,+8) + `$A6` (+8,+8) shell · `$A9` (+0,+16) + `$A8` (+8,+16) feet\n\nCross‑checked in RAM: enemy slot 1 active, **type byte `$00`**, while the two Goombas on the same frame are type `$06` — a distinct enemy, not a mislabelled Goomba. `get_region` object mode returned 213 palette‑5 pixels over CHR `$A5`–`$A9`.\n\n## Flagpole + flag — `tile`s in group `flagpole`, `sprite` id `flag`\n**Reach:** the last stretch kept killing Mario, so I stopped guessing: `$00CE` rising past 176 and wrapping is the **death animation**, not a pit (the nametable ground rows `$B4/$B5/$B6/$B7` are unbroken across every read — those four \"falls\" were Goomba hits). Writing `$079F = 200` (star timer) then running right got him to the pole in one go.\n\n**Pole (background, BG pattern table `$1000`, palette 0):**\n- `$1A2` + `$1A3` — the shaft: two 8px cells each carrying a 1px index‑1 line on the shared edge (`$1A2` right edge, `$1A3` left edge) → one 2 px green line\n- `$12F` + `$13D` — the top ball, two halves\n- **Proof:** `get_region` color mode at (109,100) = 128 pixels of bg‑palette‑0 slot 1 across CHR `0x1A2`/`0x1A3`, box (108,68)–(109,131), a 2 px vertical run, with **no other pixel in view on that slot**.\n\n**Flag:** it's a **sprite**, not background — `get_region` object at (105,175) = 136 palette‑5 sprite pixels across OAM #10–12 (CHR `$7E`,`$7F`), box (93,172)–(108,187). OAM: `$7E` (+0,+0), `$7F` (+8,+0), `$7E` (+8,+8) — a 16×16 pennant (white triangles + green/white circle), palette 5, no flips. Its y is not fixed: it rides the pole down during the slide, which is why the frame caught it at the bottom.\n\nI also recorded a `scene` for the level end (with the full reach) and a `note` on the death‑animation‑vs‑pit diagnosis. `promote_mappings` ran once: **8 discoveries promoted** (65 tiles, 9 sprites, 34 addresses in the file). Emulator is running again, mid‑level‑end.\n\nOne honest caveat: the Koopa's per‑part colour labels (head vs shell vs feet) are my reading of the tile pixel grids laid out as a 16×24 turtle; the tile IDs, offsets, flips and palette are directly observed."}
